# Voice — Read VOICE.md Before Any Copy

**READ `VOICE.md` in full before writing or editing any site copy** — homepage, case studies, project blurbs, blog posts, meta descriptions. It's the voice layer and the source of truth; this rule only summarizes it.

- First person, conversational ("I build…"), never third-person marketing.
- No buzzwords (synergy, leverage, results-driven, passionate about, best-in-class…). If it belongs in a LinkedIn influencer post, it's out.
- Ground everything in reality: every claim traces to the resume, a shipped project, or a number. Never invent.
- Numbers over adjectives. Short sentences. Plain words.
- Home page never mentions Amazon. Professional experience and personal projects stay in separate sections, always.
- No hype, no "coming soon" theater — only real, shareable things. "A project counts when a stranger can open it."

If Chirag says "this doesn't sound like me", update `VOICE.md` — don't just fix the one-off copy.
